 34AL    34MG B- DECAY:44.9 MS:XUNDL-5 2017LI03                           201811
 34AL c  Compiled (unevaluated) dataset from 2017Li03:                          
 34AL2c  Phys Rev C 95, 021301(R) (2017)                                        
 34AL c  Compiled by B. Singh (McMaster): July 27, 2017                         
 34AL c  2017Li03: {+34}Mg source formed in U(p,X),E=1.4 GeV reaction           
 34AL2c  using UC{-x} target and Proton Synchrotron Booster at ISOLDE-CERN.     
 34AL3c  The Mg atoms were selectively ionized using resonance ionization laser 
 34AL4c  ion source (RILIS), accelerated to 40 keV, then A=34 ions selected     
 34AL5c  by the ISOLDE General Purpose Separator, and finally deposited on a    
 34AL6c  movable tape located at the ISOLDE Decay station. Measured E|g, I|g,   
 34AL7c  |b particles, |b-gated |g spectra, |b-gated |g|g-coin, half-life and   
 34AL8c  %|b{+-}n for {+34}Mg decay using a plastic scintillator for |b         
 34AL9c  particles, and five HPGe clover detectors for |g detection. Deduced    
 34ALAc  levels, J|p, |b feedings and log| {Ift} values. Comparison with        
 34ALBc  large-scale shell-model calculations using the SDPF-U-MIX interaction. 
 34AL cB IB$From 2017Li03.                                                      
 34AL cB LOGFT$Deduced by compiler. Values in 2017Li03 are nearly the same.     
 34AL cG E,RI$Values are from e-mail replies of Feb 13 and 16, 2017 from        
 34AL2cG A. Negret and R. Lica (first author of 2017Li03), with systematic      
 34AL3cG uncertainty of 0.1 keV in E|g, arising from calibration of             
 34AL4cG |g-ray spectra, added in quadrature to the uncertainties listed        
 34AL5cG in the e-mail communication. |DE|g(stat) is the statistical uncertainty
 34AL6cG in keV, as communicated by authors in e-mail reply.                    
 34AL cL E$Deduced by compiler from least-squares fit to the E|g values.        
 34AL cL J$As proposed by 2017Li03, based on log| {Ift} values from 0+          
 34AL2cL parent state and shell-model predictions.                              
 34AL cL T$From 2012Ro25.                                                       
